Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Salima Shaikh  M D  Reports To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITH CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH CHEMOTHERAPY EFFECT  RARE SCATTERED MINUTE FOCI IN THE REGION OF THE SCAR  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  WITH CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH CHEMOTHERAPY EFFECT  FEW FOCI IN THE REGION OF THE SCAR  EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION PRESENT  WITHIN AND AWAY FROM THE SCAR  THE EXAMINED RESECTION MARGINS ARE NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 24 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The sizes of the lymph node metastases in this post chemotherapy specimen fall into the categories of one  isolated tumor cell  deposit and one  micrometastasis   An additional node shows a prominent scar with hemosiderin and dystrophic calcification  but no tumor cells are identified  There is no extracapsular extension or involvement of axillary vessels  Involvement of skin or dermal lymphatics is not identified  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast axilla   is a REMOVED_DATE kilogram  35 x 28 x 27cm mastectomy specimen with a 10 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tail with palpable lymph nodes  A 5 x 4cm nipple areola complex is noted on the 30 x 20cm tan white skin ellipse  which is unremarkable except for a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm telangiectic area  which is 2 6cm from the complex  The posterior aspect of the mastectomy specimen is smooth  without lesions  The anterior aspect is inked blue  the posterior aspect is inked black  and the specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral  Deep to the nipple  in the inferior central breast  is a very ill defined puckered vague area of scarring admixed with fat  measuring approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm  The changes extend to 3cm from the deep margin  There is no well defined mass lesion identified   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Deep margin  radial    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Ill defined area of scarring   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   More central aspect of scarred area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple and underlying breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional section of skin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Pinkish area from lateral breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area of tissue from medial breast with deep margin  Multiple lymph nodes are found in the axilla ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 1cm   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node  multisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Each block contains one lymph node that is bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five intact candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Six intact candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Six intact candidate lymph nodes  Gross Dictation by Salima Shaikh M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Salima Shaikh M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Negative.
