Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Radiology Outpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  STEPHANIE L  SHAPIRO  M D  PHOEBE E FREER  M D  Resident  Matija Snuderl  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 30 year old woman with epidermal nevus syndrome and right bloody nipple discharge  An MRI at a referring hospital demonstrated an enhancing mass in the right breast  An ultrasound exam demonstrated 2 hypoechoic masses  Mass A is at 9 00 o clock  Mass B is at 3 00 o clock  both are 3cm from nipple  The differential diagnosis for mass A is hamartoma versus fibroadenoma  The differential diagnosis for mass B is a cyst versus fibroadenoma versus hamartoma  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  RIGHT  9 00   CORE BIOPSY 1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE 2  COMPLEX SCLEROSING INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  SEE NOTE  B  BREAST  RIGHT  3 00   CORE BIOPSY FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH CYST WALL  NOTE  A panel of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin were performed on slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The immunostaining pattern highlights the absence of a myoepithelial layer in areas of invasive ductal carcinoma and supports the diagnosis  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  right breast 9 o clock   are multiple cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue  which is submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  right breast 3 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm core of fibrofatty tissue which is submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue  which is submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 04   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10 10 12AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  9 00  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows    Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells    Show moderate  2   ove