 node candidates  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  The lymph node candidates are entirely submitted as   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   6 intact lymph node candidates   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 intact lymph node candidates  1 is inked black and 1 is inked blue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 intact lymph node candidates  1 is inked black  and 1 is inked blue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 lymph node candidates  1 is inked black and 1 is inked blue  the inked nodes are bisected    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 bisected lymph node candidates  1 is inked blue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 intact lymph node candidates  1 is inked black   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 bisected lymph node candidates  1 is inked black   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node candidate  serially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node candidate  serially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional intact lymph node candidates  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 14   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 09 36 20PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  Rare tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells 