t on blood thinners     Social History   Tobacco use  No   Alcohol use  No     Past Medical History   No personal history of malignancy     Review of Patient Data in the EMR   Radiology  Yes   Past Histology  No   Office Notes  Yes     Physical Examination  Laterality was established according to departmental    universal protocol  Examination of the left breast reveals a 1 2cm  firm   mobile mass     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and complications were explained to the patient and  written consent was obtained  3 aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles  without anesthesia and without complications  4 slides were stained for  immediate evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further evaluation     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were discussed with the  patient  The preliminary results were communicated to Dr  Hughes in person at  4 55 p m         The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Joseph Misdraji MD on REMOVED_DATE 10 04       CLINICAL HISTORY  36 year old female with history of intraductal papillomas with left breast mass  at 9 o clock         SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Received 4 slides in ETOH and 1 air dried slide   4ccs clear  colorless fluid  1 SurePath          Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT       report_end  , Negative.
